{"availability":"available","full":"blakeshao/a-psychos-gd-tool","name":"a-psychos-gd-tool","description":"a node-based graphic design tool","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":136,"forks":11,"created":"2026-06-11T20:27:03Z","updated":"2026-08-07T14:05:30Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://a-psychos-gd-tool.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://a-psychos-gd-tool.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:30.215Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:30.215Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:30.215Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:08:30.215Z","stars":136,"forks":11}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Hosted version: a-psychos-gd-tool.vercel.app — needs a WebGPU browser (Chrome/Edge 113+ or Safari 18+).","A node-based graphic design tool that runs in the browser, on the GPU. You build a poster by wiring nodes on a canvas: text is shaped into vector outlines, vectors are warped and combined, rasters are blurred and dithered — every conversion is an explicit node on a typed wire, never a hidden coercion. The engine only re-computes what a change actually touches, so dragging a parameter stays interactive even in deep graphs.","Status: experimental, under active development. 35 node types; undo/redo is built in (⌘/Ctrl Z, ⇧⌘/Ctrl Z); persistence is not built yet (see Roadmap)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/blakeshao/a-psychos-gd-tool/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"72763413019b0bd37e320d5489aa69d4936fd82de2eb8e8fdcadf5a16e204f4c","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:30.367Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:08:30.367Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Hosted version: a-psychos-gd-tool.vercel.app — needs a WebGPU browser (Chrome/Edge 113+ or Safari 18+).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/blakeshao/a-psychos-gd-tool/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"72763413019b0bd37e320d5489aa69d4936fd8